.git
node_modules
app/node_modules
app/.next
data
*.duckdb
docs/superpowers
.superpowers
# Generated by `tsc --noEmit` and by `next build`, gitignored, and NOT tracked -- so leaving them
# in the build context makes the image depend on whether this host happens to have run
# `make app-check`. Measured: one `make app-check` rewrites app/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo, which
# invalidates `COPY app ./app`, which re-runs `next build`, which mints a fresh build id -- so the
# next `make image` produced a DIFFERENT image from an unchanged tree. Both files are regenerated
# inside the build stage; nothing needs the host's copy. Measurement and the two-direction mutant:
# docs/architecture/hosting.md, "The build context must contain only tracked files".
**/*.tsbuildinfo
app/next-env.d.ts
# TRACKED, and excluded for the other reason: nothing in the image needs it. smoke.sh runs on the
# HOST in both modes (container mode drives the container from outside), and `next build` never
# reads it -- but it lives under app/, so every edit to it invalidated `COPY app ./app`, re-ran
# `next build`, minted a fresh build id and moved the image's `.Size` -- which is how a COMMENT-ONLY
# edit to this file silently staled the size figure written down in docs/architecture/hosting.md one
# commit earlier. Two-direction mutant, BUILD_SHA pinned so the ignore entry is the only variable:
# hosting.md § "The build context must contain only tracked files".
app/smoke.sh
